Z||000002||88formula||06-14-2000||04:51 PM||||WOW! What kind of 3.4 do you have in that fiero? I didn't know that .6 liters increase in displacement could make that much of a difference.<P> To bad you don't live near me because I am modifying my 2.8-liter with a whole bunch of go fast goodies and I would like to race you to see if I could hang with a 3.4 fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ThatRickGuy||06-14-2000||05:42 PM||||88formula, I've heard of people, on this very form actually, trying the same conversion, a few days ago there was the debate over a turbo 2.8 or a non-turbo 3.4, I think the numbers were abound 200 for the 2.6 and 180 for the 3.4. Either way you line it up, that's a lot of ponies for a car that weighs arround 2700 lbs. I mean, my '76 lemans has arround 200 hp, but it weighs almost 2 1/2 tons!||||reg||1
Z||000004||87PegasusGT||06-14-2000||06:45 PM||||I should be pulling about 200hp with my mods.<BR>The torque is where the 3.4 will probably take you. That Vette would have toasted me on the freeway, but dang it pulled ahead SO slowly from 20mph that I HAVE to see where I stand Versus a standard Vette.||||reg||1
Z||000005||87ECO5||06-14-2000||07:31 PM||||If that was, in fact, a 40th anniversary Corvette, then you <I>DID</I> race a standard Vette.  1993 was the 40th anniversary of the car and, other than special paint, it shared everything with the other "non-ZR1" Vettes - including the 300 horsepower LT1.<P>If you're sure it was a '97, then you were competing against an LS1 with 345 horsepower.<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 06-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||turbo86se||06-14-2000||07:31 PM||||Early last summer, I toasted a low 90's Vette at a stop light. The Vette had a head start (wasn't really paying attention), I nailed the throttle, with very little turbo lag, my 86SE was very quickly next to him, then he was completely in my side-view mirror. The only thing he said to me at the next light was "What the he!! you got in that thing!!?"  I was smiling from ear to ear for hours!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||87PegasusGT||06-15-2000||01:10 PM||||It wasn't a C5. I thought the slightly different body style made it a newer model. That would explain why it was so close. See, last night I had a run in with a C5. It was at a light and some idiot in a newer Eclipse turbo was revving. I of course got in between knowing I would get smoked by the Vette. I actually took both of them to 40 but after that, the C5 ripped by me even faster than I could increase the distance btw me and the Eclipse. He he he.... I hope the Eclipse driver felt foolish.....||||reg||1
Z||000008||88formula||06-15-2000||06:04 PM||||All you need now 87PegasusGT, is a turbo and you would keep your lead on those C5 corvettes in a drag race. You have to take that beast to the track to see what you can get for 1/4-mile times. <P>To bad you don't live near me! Mine is not a turbocharged 2.8 and according to simulations run on my Desktop Dyno program, I should have around 180 HP at 5500 RPM and good low end torque to help me off the line, more than a stock 2.8.  <P>maybe some day I will have a chance to drag a 3.4 fiero to see how well I do.||||reg||1
